6 april is national donate a life month  it's a time to spread awareness about  organ eye and tissue donation mary jane  bellies alive this morning at nevada  donor network with a local mother's  message of donation mary jane good  morning  good morning to you john it's been over  five years since eileen gilbeau donated  her kidney to her daughter haley she  says her daughter is healthy and  thriving and wants to educate the  community on becoming an organ donor as  she knows not everyone is as lucky to  get a match haley dale was just 17 years  old when her kidneys started to fail and  she had to start dialysis luckily she  only had to wait a year for a kidney  transplant as her mom was a match while  the process was lengthy and full of  anticipation eileen says it's rewarding  to see the impact of the donation not  just for the recipient but for the donor  too  i had no energy you know i was  going to high school at the time and  working  and having dialysis you know three four  times a week so it was draining you know  and and very exhausting so just having  that energy back so quickly just shows  how sick i was and what a difference it  made so i think that alone is  is worth it you know to donate seeing  that person just back to being a hundred  percent i would just encourage everybody  to donate um it is it is truly you know  life-changing not just for the recipient  but you know the donor as well i mean i  can't even  imagine  um what she would be suffering you know  had it not been for that for that  donation  eileen says if you want to become a  donor it's important to stay on top of  your health and review all your options  and if you'd like to learn more  information there are a number of  resources available to you here in the  community including this one at the  nevada donor network and we'll be sure  to post a link for you on our website at  eightnewsnow.com reporting live from  sahara in burnham mary jane balleza live  local now
 

